  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia - Winery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Neerlands Wijnmakerij Participaties BV will research the feasibility of large-scale wine production and wine leisure activities nearby Cartagena, Colombia. By planting and testing different grape varieties in a pilot project of 2ha in two years&#x2019; time they seek confirmation that sustainable high quality grape growing in the Colombian climate and soil is possible. With the production of some excellent trail wine varieties in the winery they want to determine whether grape cultivation is economically profitable at the chosen location in Colombia. The expertise will be shared with small holders so that they also can start cultivating grapes that can be processed in the new winery.The winery will generate new employment opportunities for (female) young (18+) Colombians. With this project Colombia has the opportunity to develop a domestic high margin wine market instead of importing wine in high quantities from Chile and Argentina.</narrative>
  </description>
